    "note.5-1.quay": "Every rope has a tide at its end.",
    "note.5-1.bell": "The bells know the water better than the map.",
    "note.5-2.flood": "The low town is below every calculation.",
    "note.5-2.return": "The old flood has found a new street.",
    "note.5-3.barge": "Corentin opens one gate, outside every hour.",
    "note.5-4.corentin": "I was taught that the map is right.",
    "note.5-4.key": "The Chancellor's key bears the first borne's mark.",
    "note.6-1.archives": "Every shelf is a road when the clerk says so.",
    "note.6-2.scales": "The register closes from the edges inward.",
    "note.6-3.allies": "Old names answer from the margins.",
    "note.6-4.ilse": "I do not want to win. I want the winning to end.",
    "note.6-4.registre": "Even I obey the Right of Passage.",
    "note.6-4.white": "The white cell remembers what the map erased.",
    "note.6-4.signature": "A signature can seal a world, and erase its signer.",
